WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:02.804
(gentle music)

00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:10.919
♪ Unforgettable ♪

00:00:10.919 --> 00:00:15.919
♪ That's what you are ♪

00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:22.683
♪ Unforgettable ♪

00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:27.683
♪ Though near or far ♪

00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:35.122
♪ Like a song of love that clings to me ♪

00:00:35.906 --> 00:00:40.906
♪ How the thoughts of
you does things to me ♪

00:00:42.244 --> 00:00:47.244
♪ Never before ♪

00:00:47.606 --> 00:00:52.606
♪ Has someone been more ♪

00:00:53.002 --> 00:00:57.045
♪ Unforgettable ♪

00:00:57.045 --> 00:01:02.045
♪ In every way ♪

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:09.414
♪ And forevermore that's how you'll stay ♪

00:01:16.123 --> 00:01:21.123
♪ That's why darling it's incredible ♪

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.400
♪ That someone so unforgettable ♪

00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:32.792
♪ Thinks that I am unforgettable too ♪

00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:38.137
(gentle music)

00:01:39.812 --> 00:01:42.812
(audience cheering)

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:51.836
- All right, all right, everybody,

00:01:51.836 --> 00:01:54.075
welcome to "The Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:01:54.075 --> 00:01:57.035
it's Martin Luther King Jr Day.

00:01:57.035 --> 00:01:59.013
Give it up for my band y'all.

00:01:59.013 --> 00:02:02.350
(audience cheering)

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:06.180
That was "Unforgettable" by Nat King Cole

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.700
who was an outspoken voice
in civil rights movement

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.950
as well as just one of
the greatest artists ever.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:14.310
He was the first African-American
to host a network TV show,

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.940
I did not know that, I thought
that was cool information.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.770
Throughout his career, he sued hotels

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.240
that wouldn't let him stay the night,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.050
and in 1963, he marched on
Washington with Dr. King.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.250
Before his passing,

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.647
Martin Luther King Jr actually
wrote him a telegram saying,

00:02:29.647 --> 00:02:33.330
"You have my constant prayers,
I will be indebted to you

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.830
for your support in the struggle."

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.380
Which is an incredible
thing I didn't know as well.

